1. jQuery EFFECT METHOD WITH CALLBACK FUNCTION

Create:
Pract9.html

CODE:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Basic jQuery</title>
<script src="jquery-3.6.1.min.js"></script>
<script>
$(document).ready(function () {
    $("button").click(function () {
        $("p").hide("slow", function () {
            alert("The paragraph is now hidden");
        });
    });
});
</script>
</head>
<body>

<p>Aanchal:269704</p>
<p>Welcome to MCC</p>

<button>Click!</button>
</body>
</html>


OUTPUT:
Initially:

Aanchal:269704
Welcome to MCC
Click!

After clicking Click!:

The paragraph is now hidden

The paragraph gets hidden and the callback function displays the alert.


2. jQuery TO GET AND SET TEXT CONTENT

CODE:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Basic jQuery</title>
<script src="jquery-3.6.1.min.js"></script>
<script>
$(document).ready(function(){
    $("#b1").click(function(){
        var str=$("p").text();
        alert(str);
    });
    $("#b2").click(function(){
        $("p").text("Hello World");
    });
});
</script>
</head>
<body>
<p>Aanchal:269704</p>
<p>MongoDB</p>
<button id="b1">Get</button>
<button id="b2">Set</button>
</body>
</html>


OUTPUT:
Aanchal:269704
MongoDB

Get → Displays the text inside the paragraph in an alert.
Set → Changes the paragraph text to:

Hello World


3. jQuery TO GET AND SET HTML CONTENT

CODE:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Basic jQuery</title>
<script src="jquery-3.6.1.min.js"></script>
<script>
$(document).ready(function(){
    $("#b1").click(function(){
        var str=$("p").html();
        alert(str);
    });
    $("#b2").click(function(){
        $("p").html("<b>Hello World</b>");
    });
});
</script>
</head>
<body>
<p><b>Aanchal:</b> <u>269704</u></p>
<p>MongoDB</p>
<button id="b1">Get</button>
<button id="b2">Set</button>
</body>
</html>


OUTPUT:
Aanchal:269704
MongoDB

Get → Gets the HTML content of the paragraph.

Set → Changes the paragraph content to:

Hello World

"Hello World" appears in bold because <b> is used.


